Aeternum Engine - Runtime folder guide
======================================
This folder is the per-config runtime output (example: build\bin\RelWithDebInfo).
The helper scripts START_SERVER.bat / STOP_SERVER.bat / STATUS.bat / CHECK_CONFIG.bat
are generated here by CMake on every build. Do not invent a separate server\ tree.

This README is English-only by design. It lists the technologies this build uses
and how to configure/start the isolated Aeternum stack. It never documents
passwords, tokens, or non-local network addresses.


1) Technologies to download / install (versions used by THIS build)
-------------------------------------------------------------------
- Git                          - clone and update the source tree
- CMake                        - @AETERNUM_CMAKE_VERSION@
- Visual Studio 2022           - @AETERNUM_VS_VERSION@
                                 (Desktop development with C++ / MSVC toolset)
- Visual C++ Redistributable   - matching VS 2022 x64 (for machines that only run binaries)
- MySQL Community Server 8.0.x - @AETERNUM_MYSQL_VERSION@
                                 Aeternum uses TCP port 3308 (keep other stacks on their own ports)
- OpenSSL 3.x                  - @AETERNUM_OPENSSL_VERSION@
                                 CMake also copies legacy.dll next to the executables
                                 (OpenSSL 3.x legacy provider; silences 'failed to load legacy.dll')
- Boost                        - @AETERNUM_BOOST_VERSION@
- Python 3.x                   - @AETERNUM_PYTHON_VERSION@
                                 (optional; needed only for some contrib/tools scripts)

Optional on the build machine: a full Visual Studio 2022 Build Tools or IDE install
with the MSVC v143 toolset and Windows 10/11 SDK.


2) Database setup
-----------------
Create the isolated Aeternum schemas (names must stay aeternum_* so they never
collide with other local stacks):

  auth
  characters
  world
  hotfixes

A starter SQL script is copied next to this README as create_aeternum_dbs.sql.
Run it with your local MySQL client against the instance that listens on port 3308.
Grant a dedicated DB user of your choosing; put that user into the *.conf files
locally. Do not commit credentials.

Then import / update base SQL from the source tree (sql\ and any project-specific

After importing auth SQL, set the realm display name to Aeternum
(contrib/aeternum/sql/set_realm_name_aeternum.sql, or UPDATE realmlist SET name='Aeternum').
Do not leave the default upstream name 'Trinity' on this stack.
updates) into those four databases following the normal TrinityCore-style order
(auth -> characters -> world -> hotfixes, plus updates).


3) Config setup
---------------
After a build, this folder contains:

  bnetserver.conf.dist
  worldserver.conf.dist

Copy each to the same name without .dist if the .conf does not exist yet:

  copy bnetserver.conf.dist  bnetserver.conf
  copy worldserver.conf.dist worldserver.conf

Edit the .conf files locally:
- Database connection lines for aeternum_* on port 3308
- WorldServerPort / BattlenetPort / LoginREST.Port (defaults for this isolated stack
  are World 18085, Battlenet 2119, LoginREST 18083 ? different from other local stacks)
- LogsDir = "logs"   (relative folder created beside the executables)
- DataDir / client data paths as required on your machine
- LoginREST certificate paths (see below)

Certificates / PEM files used by LoginREST and bnet are LOCAL ONLY.
They are not stored in git. Place the PEM files this machine needs next to the
binaries (or point the conf keys at your local cert paths).


4) How to start / stop / status / check
---------------------------------------
From THIS folder:

  CHECK_CONFIG.bat   - runs worldserver.exe --check-config
  START_SERVER.bat   - TCP-checks MySQL 3308, starts bnet, waits for ports from conf,
                       starts world, waits, prints PIDs/ports (never prints passwords)
  STATUS.bat         - shows listen state for conf ports and processes whose path is
                       under this folder; optional health probe if AETERNUM_HEALTH_TOKEN
                       is set in the environment
  STOP_SERVER.bat    - graceful stop of ONLY processes whose executable path is under
                       this folder, with a 120s IT+EN countdown, then force-kill if needed

Do not point these scripts at another stack's install folder.

4b) Admin API token (localhost :9300)
-------------------------------------
Admin HTTP binds to 127.0.0.1 only. Never expose port 9300.

Token precedence (resolved at worldserver start / conf reload):
  1) Environment variable named by Admin.TokenFromEnv
     (if Admin.TokenFromEnv is empty -> AETERNUM_ADMIN_TOKEN)
  2) Else Admin.Token from worldserver.conf (PLAINTEXT — deprecated)
If Admin.Token is non-empty in conf, the server logs a WARN without the value.
Fail-fast for conf tokens is planned for a later version.
Default Admin.TokenMinLength = 32.
Operator token is OPTIONAL (Admin.OperatorTokenFromEnv / AETERNUM_ADMIN_OPERATOR_TOKEN).

Per-instance: set a distinct Admin.TokenFromEnv in that instance's conf so two
installations under the same Windows user do not share one token.

Wizard (shipped beside the binaries):
  Manage-AeternumAdminToken.ps1 -Action Generate|Rotate|Recover -RuntimeDir <this folder>
  Uses RandomNumberGenerator; shows the token once; User-scope env; never logs the value.
  Rotate/Recover restart THIS instance only when you pass -ConfirmRestart
  (path-scoped stop with 120s IT+EN countdown). Does not touch Trinity or other instances.



5) Ports (isolated Aeternum defaults)
-------------------------------------
  MySQL          3308
  Battlenet      2119   (bnetserver.conf -> BattlenetPort)
  LoginREST      18083  (bnetserver.conf -> LoginREST.Port)
  World          18085  (worldserver.conf -> WorldServerPort)

Always re-read the values from the .conf files; STATUS.bat and START_SERVER.bat do.


6) Logs
-------
Default LogsDir for this layout:  .\logs
(relative to this runtime folder). Check Server.log, DB errors, and bnet logs there.


7) Troubleshooting
------------------
- Launcher / LoginREST certificate errors:
  Confirm the PEM/chain files referenced by LoginREST.* and bnetserver cert/key
  settings exist locally and match what the launcher trusts. Certs are not in git.

- "Missing build auth key" / error 70790 style failures:
  For local lab use you may set Network.SkipBuildAuthKeyCheck = 1 in worldserver.conf.
  Do not enable that on a public realm.

- Warning 'OpenSSL failed to load legacy.dll':
  Rebuild so POST_BUILD copies OpenSSL's bin\legacy.dll next to worldserver/bnetserver.
  Do not set OPENSSL_MODULES unless you know you need a custom modules path.

- CHECK_CONFIG fails:
  Fix database connectivity, missing DataDir files, or conf syntax, then re-run.

- START_SERVER fails on MySQL 3308:
  Start the MySQL 8.0 service and confirm it listens on 3308.

- Wrong processes stopped:
  STOP_SERVER only targets bnetserver.exe / worldserver.exe whose path is under
  this folder. Other stacks in different directories are left alone.

- Ports already in use:
  Ensure no other process holds 2119 / 18083 / 18085, or change the conf ports.


8) CMake regeneration
---------------------
Templates live in source under contrib/aeternum/scripts/*.bat.in and README.txt.in.
Building worldserver/bnetserver copies the generated files into this runtime directory
automatically (POST_BUILD). Rebuild after editing templates.

Generated by CMake for Aeternum Engine.


